{
 "manifest_version": 1,
 "semantics": [
  "Allocate every buffer in `buffers` once and initialize it from its owner workload's init; later bundles that name the same buffer share it (state persists across admissions).",
  "An admission may start (list order breaks ties) when: time since start >= at_us (if set), every bundle in after_bundles has completed, and for each entry of `when` the live version of that variable is in [min, max] (max omitted = unbounded). Several admissions may be in flight at once; priority and deadline_us are inside the tasks.",
  "base_versions are the live versions of the variables at admission and bundle_dir was compiled with them. For a variable the admission does not publish (publishes lacks it) the value is only a minimum: use the live version if it is higher (a reader of weights >= v compiles against whatever is live). When bundle_dir is null, or the live version differs, compile `compile.workload` with the live versions (compile_workload.py --base-versions) or add the offset in the executor.",
  "A bundle's publishes advance the variable by `publishes[var]`; the live version after completion = base + that.",
  "manifest_version 2 only: an admission with a `guard` {buffer, index, cmp, value} additionally needs the comparison of that buffer element (read when it would otherwise start) to hold; otherwise it is skipped, as is every admission naming a skipped one in after_bundles. A guarded admission publishes nothing."
 ],
